<title>RUSSIA: Kazakhstan may double Eurobond to $200 mln.</title>
<headline>Kazakhstan may double Eurobond to $200 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan is considering doubling the size of its planned Eurobond to $200 million at the request of potential investors, Prime Minister Akezhan Kazhegeldin said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He told a news conference in Moscow that the Central Asian state's debut Eurobond would be launched after December 4.</p>
</text>
